vim's buffers seem to always have at least one line (see the Related issue for a discussion about potentially changing this), so we can't create an empty buffer and then add lines one by one to it. That results in an extra line at the top. Visible with the following config:

```lua
require'fidget'.setup {
	notification = {
		window = {
			border = "rounded",
			winblend = 0,
		},
	},
}
```

The fix is to `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines` all the empty lines we'll need at once.

Related: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/34272
Fixes: 2635400d77bf ("feat: render notifications with extmarks")
